# Change detection verified across two boots — 2026-09-09

## Run 1 — hash inputs changed by the rebuild, so a repaint is expected
=== wake 1 (power-on) ===
  batt: 92%
  fetch: weather ok, air ok, launch none
  runway: 92 days until recharge
  draw: repainting, hash 11bc5646 -> c64d8bbb
  draw: full refresh took 37937 ms
sleeping 1993 s (0.6 h)

## Run 2 — same data, power-cycled; the stored hash matches
=== wake 1 (power-on) ===
  batt: 92%
  fetch: weather ok, air ok, launch none
  runway: 92 days until recharge
  draw: skipped, content unchanged (hash c64d8bbb)
sleeping 1917 s (0.5 h)

Run 1 took ~48 s including a 37.9 s refresh; run 2 took ~10 s and never
touched the panel. The hash survived a power cycle, so the NVS copy works,
not just the RTC one.
